From: Tessel <noreply@nobaraproject.org>
Subject: [PATCH] remove the shortcuts-inhibit listener at shutdown

The keyboard-shortcuts-inhibit patch added a new_inhibitor listener and
never removed it. wlroots asserts that a manager's signals have no
listeners left when the display is destroyed, so every exit of the
compositor (signing out, the greeter handing over to a session) ended in
SIGABRT.
---
diff --git a/src/server.c b/src/server.c
index a1d21bc..b188477 100644
--- a/src/server.c
+++ b/src/server.c
@@ -930,6 +930,7 @@ server_finish(void)
 	kde_server_decoration_finish();
 	xdg_server_decoration_finish();
 	wl_list_remove(&server.new_constraint.link);
+	wl_list_remove(&server.new_keyboard_shortcuts_inhibitor.link);
 	wl_list_remove(&server.output_power_manager_set_mode.link);
 	wl_list_remove(&server.tearing_new_object.link);
 	if (server.drm_lease_request.notify) {
